## What I Learned

### Incremental Development Works Best

Implementing one feature at a time makes debugging easier and prevents introducing multiple issues simultaneously.

### Testing is Part of Development

Every completed feature should be verified before continuing to the next milestone.

### Documentation Matters

Keeping documentation updated alongside implementation makes future development and collaboration much easier.

### Small Wins Build Large Projects

Complex applications are created through many small, validated milestones—not one massive coding session.

